  "definition": "MSP refers to the Marchigian Sardinian alcohol-preferring rat, a preclinical research strain used to model vulnerability to alcohol use disorder. In the supplied source, these rats show disturbed sleep and wake patterns that resemble some changes seen in people with alcohol-related problems.",
